<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) & Meinhardt (1993, 2012) Hydra vulgaris activator-inhibitor morphogenesis, head regeneration, tentacle ring & coupled three-system 3D shell — Code-to-model traceability: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring (L1-131) maps every section to its equations and figures, including a new §2b that writes out the three-system equations, the operator, the analytic threshold and what the shell does and does not reproduce; every shell function carries a docstring naming its role; the math KG now registers 7 laws with Lean and code loci that were re-pinned to the current line numbers. Deductions: the three-system coupling functions cite Meinhardt (1993) by section title (\"how to form structures close to each other\") rather than equation (-4); the kappa_head saturation, Hill exponents and the `1e-5..250` clipping are untraced numerical choices (-3); the Pass 2 docstring statistics were stale until this pass (now corrected), which shows the docstring is not generated from the measurements (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1972-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor.py L913–L923: tentacle_drive / foot_drive docstrings state the functional form and its purpose but cite no equation of Meinhardt (1993) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/4d5512d/1972-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor.py#L913-L923>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) & Meinhardt (1993, 2012) Hydra vulgaris activator-inhibitor morphogenesis, head regeneration, tentacle ring & coupled three-system 3D shell — Model fidelity to source: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) part is unchanged and exact: steady state, Jacobian, d_c = (sqrt(2)+1)^2, dispersion (L187-268), 1D column / bisection / ring (L298-533), backed by 3 Lean theorems. Pass 3 adds the requested mechanism: three coupled activator-inhibitor loops plus source density on a 3D surface of revolution with the correct Laplace-Beltrami operator (L827-886, L925-978), each loop given a stable off state by basal inhibitor production so that the tentacle band and the foot are placed by an analytic threshold w_c (L808-825) that the self-test verifies against the simulated band (L1964-1965). Deductions: the coupling functions and all 20 coefficients in THREE_SYSTEM_PARAMS (L788-799) are the script's reduced forms, cited to Meinhardt (1993) only qualitatively, not the paper's appendix equations (-4); the shell is finite-difference with fixed geometry, not the finite-element shell the v2 item asked for (-2); the foot -> source-density feedback of Meinhardt's scheme is absent and the sigma equation relaxes to a prescribed exp(-4s/L) profile (-2); Meinhardt's tentacle-first regeneration is not reproduced because tentacle gating requires sigma to rise under the new head first (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1972-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor.py L788–L799: THREE_SYSTEM_PARAMS: 20 coefficients and Hill constants chosen by this implementation, not digitised from Meinhardt (1993) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/4d5512d/1972-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor.py#L788-L799>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) & Meinhardt (1993, 2012) Hydra vulgaris activator-inhibitor morphogenesis, head regeneration, tentacle ring & coupled three-system 3D shell — Morphometric validation: 89/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1691-1856) now returns 14 measurements. The 7 Pass 2 metrics keep their literature / specimen references; the 7 new shell metrics include three with genuine specimen references (ring offset 0.111 vs 0.070 +- 0.081, tentacle count 7 vs 6, spacing 0.091 vs 0.084 of body length) and an analytic-vs-simulated consistency check (ring inside the phi_t > w_c band). Deductions: four new metrics carry model-internal or trivially satisfied reference values — the foot reference (L-1)/L (L1748), the ablation reference = the default run's own leak (L1758), the Spearman references 1.0 (L1768) and the regeneration recovery reference 1.0 (L1778) — so they validate internal behaviour, not biology (-6); the spacing agreement is the calibration target, not a validation (-2); no uncertainty across seeds or specimens is reported for any shell metric (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1972-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor.py L1744–L1783: Foot, ablation, Spearman and regeneration measurements use model-internal reference values rather than literature or specimen numbers <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/4d5512d/1972-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor.py#L1744-L1783>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-measurement-3d-shell-amputation-s-l-2-hypostome-recovery-at-the-fragment-tip-and-head-before-ring-ordering>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-measurement-3d-shell-foot-activator-position-and-head-foot-axial-separation>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-measurement-3d-shell-hypostome-cap-azimuthal-coefficient-of-variation-cv-theta-a-at-the-apex>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-measurement-3d-shell-sub-hypostomal-tentacle-ring-axial-offset-s-ring-l-vs-specimen-attachment-offset>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-measurement-3d-shell-tentacle-primordia-count-on-the-ring-vs-hydra-vulgaris-specimen>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-measurement-ablation-kappa-a-0-no-head-tentacle-suppression-tentacle-activator-leak-into-the-hypostome>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-measurement-allometric-domain-length-scaling-correlation-r-l-n-peaks>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-measurement-body-length-sweep-spearman-monotonicity-of-tentacle-number-with-shell-size>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-measurement-equal-diffusion-negative-control-d-a-d-h-0-015-activator-spatial-std>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-measurement-gierer-meinhardt-critical-diffusivity-ratio-d-c-sqrt-2-1-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-measurement-homogeneous-steady-state-activator-concentration-a-rho-0-0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-measurement-intact-hydra-polar-column-apical-hypostome-peak-cell-index-n-40>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-measurement-sub-hypostomal-periodic-ring-tentacle-primordia-count-vs-hydra-vulgaris-specimen>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-measurement-surgical-bisection-basal-fragment-head-regeneration-recovery-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) & Meinhardt (1993, 2012) Hydra vulgaris activator-inhibitor morphogenesis, head regeneration, tentacle ring & coupled three-system 3D shell — MorphoEval overall 89.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `1972-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor.py` (89.5/100, down 2.1 from 91.6 in Pass 2). The v2 remediation item is closed in a reduced, honestly labelled form: the 1D column and ring are now accompanied by a coupled head / tentacle / foot activator-inhibitor model on a finite-difference surface of revolution whose radius profile is measured on the vendored Hydra vulgaris specimen. The shell reproduces an azimuthally uniform hypostome cap (CV_theta = 0.002), one sub-hypostomal tentacle ring of 7 primordia at s/L = 0.111 (specimen attachment band 0.070 +- 0.081; 6 tentacles), a uniform basal foot (head-foot separation 0.99 L), a monotone basal shift of the ring with the head->tentacle suppression kappa_a (Spearman rho = 1.0) with tentacle activator leaking into the hypostome when kappa_a = 0 (x~15), a monotone increase of tentacle number with body size (rho = 0.97), and after amputation at L/2 a regenerated hypostome (98 %) followed by a new ring below it. The remediation also exposed and fixed provenance defects that v2 had not caught (JSON regimes block, docstring statistics, environment versions), and the remaining gaps are structural: reduced coupling forms, declared scale calibration, no FEM / remodelling, head-first regeneration, model-internal reference values for some new measurements. Overall 89.5/100 (faithfulness 88.7, reproducibility 91.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 4d5512d; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 91, Morphological realism / specimen match 87, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 89, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 90, Reproducibility package 92. Output judged: docs/media/hydra_activator_inhibitor_comparison.png: rendered output of 1972-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor.py at 4d5512d, image/png, 1290720 B, 2227×3037 px, artifact_sha256 e0c4e97130d2627ad31b6cf098d20e0b26bcc7658a7b2fcd94ffe4d9c9d8bc3d (sha256 e0c4e97130d2627ad31b6cf098d20e0b26bcc7658a7b2fcd94ffe4d9c9d8bc3d), spec_fingerprint 49a5051749b0c67e34c6eeaa4fb8201bc071879dc58596403d8aa74086bc42c4. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 49a5051749b0c67e34c6eeaa4fb8201bc071879dc58596403d8aa74086bc42c4; artifact_sha256: e0c4e97130d2627ad31b6cf098d20e0b26bcc7658a7b2fcd94ffe4d9c9d8bc3d; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/hydra_activator_inhibitor/hydra_activator_inhibitor_reference.json=21cb10a1cf38b4c9..., datasets/hydra_activator_inhibitor/hydra_vulgaris_specimen.jpg=007d127bcfa8501d..., datasets/hydra_activator_inhibitor/paper_citations.bib=49b5c0a5531a00fe..., datasets/hydra_activator_inhibitor/scout_manifest.json=b57d0d923283daaf...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-hydra-activator-inhibitor-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) Eqs. (15a)-(15b): short-range autocatalytic activator a^2/h with long-range inhibitor; a shallow source gradient yields a single apical peak (Fig. 2); removing the apical half lets the basal fragment regenerate a peak at its cut end (Fig. 3) | Meinhardt (1993): hypostome, tentacles and foot are generated by separate activator-inhibitor systems coupled through a slowly adapting source density; tentacle activation requires a high source density and is locally suppressed by the head activator (so tentacles form at the border of the hypostome); the foot forms where the source density is lowest; fragments regenerate a hypostome and a new tentacle ring | Meinhardt (2012): review of the same three-system scheme including size-dependent and regeneration behaviour; reconstructed_in_script: Exact homogeneous steady state, Jacobian, d_c = (sqrt(2)+1)^2 and dispersion relation; 1D polar column (N = 40) with apical dominance; surgical bisection with 87.4 % head recovery; periodic 64-cell tentacle ring (6 peaks) with equal-diffusion control, diffusivity-ratio and domain-length sweeps; computer-vision segmentation of the vendored specimen (6 tentacles) | Pass 3: the specimen's body-column radius profile, tentacle-attachment ring and inter-tentacle spacing; a finite-difference Laplace-Beltrami shell (90 x 64) on that surface of revolution; reduced head / tentacle / foot Gierer-Meinhardt loops with basal inhibitor production (analytic firing threshold w_c = 0.1633) and a head-raised source density; kappa_a sweep with kappa_a = 0 ablation, body-length sweep, amputation at L/2 with head/ring regeneration timeline; 14 quantitative measurements; transfer_boundary: The three-system couplings (Hill gating sigma^8/(0.6^8 + sigma^8), suppression 1/(1 + kappa_a a), foot drive 1/(1 + (sigma/0.03)^2), sigma dynamics c_sigma a - mu_sigma (sigma - sigma_0)) and all coefficients are this script's reduced choices calibrated to reproduce the qualitative Meinhardt (1993) layout; they are not digitised from the paper's appendix equations | The shell body length L = 90 cells is a declared scale calibration (model tentacle spacing ~8.1 cells vs specimen spacing 0.084 of body length), so the tentacle COUNT (7 vs specimen 6) is a geometric consequence, not an independent prediction; the ring axial offset (0.111 vs 0.070 +- 0.081), uniform hypostome cap, basal foot and head-before-ring regeneration order are uncalibrated predictions | The 1D ring (N_ring = 64, lambda ~10.7 cells, 6 peaks) and the shell ring (lambda ~8.1 cells) use the same D_b, D_c but select different wavelengths; the 1D '6 tentacles' therefore also rests on an (undeclared in v2) circumference calibration | Specimen references are measured on a 2D projection of a tilted, contracted polyp and used as bands, not exact targets; there is one specimen and one seed; does_not_claim: A finite-element mesh, wound closure or tissue remodelling (the regenerated head on the wide cut surface is a localised spot, CV_theta = 0.95, not a cap), Meinhardt's tentacle-before-hypostome regeneration order (the model gives t_head < t_ring), the foot -> source-density negative feedback, budding, or a quantitative size series for tentacle number." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 1972-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor.py:1049-1095 — the regenerated head on the wide, un-remodelled cut surface is a localised spot (CV_theta = 0.95) and the model regenerates head before ring (t_head = 450 < t_ring = 1050), contrary to Meinhardt's (1993) tentacle-first prediction. Add wound closure (taper the fragment tip radius over time) and a tentacle gating that does not require sigma to rise under the new head, then test the regeneration order explicitly.",
        "remediation needed: 1972-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor.py:1146-1166 and 1740 — the body-length sweep count skips 6 (5 -> 7) and all shell results come from a single seed; report tentacle count and ring offset across >= 5 seeds and a finer L grid so the specimen's 6 is bracketed with an uncertainty, not a single run.",
        "remediation needed: 1972-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor.py:169-172 — the reference JSON is hashed at runtime but not pinned in EXPECTED_SHA256, so the parity block can drift silently; pin it (update the digest when the JSON changes) and have measure_outputs report a mismatch.",
        "remediation needed: 1972-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor.py:1744-1783 — four new measurements use model-internal reference values ((L-1)/L for the foot, the default run's own leak for the ablation, 1.0 for the Spearman and recovery metrics). Replace them with literature values (e.g. foot/peduncle position and tentacle number vs body size from a Hydra size series) or label them explicitly as internal consistency checks in the measurement names.",
        "remediation needed: 1972-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor.py:695-785 — specimen references depend on hand-set thresholds (tissue fraction 0.98, +0.5 px distance tolerance, 28 deg basal sector) measured on one obliquely photographed polyp; report their sensitivity (vary the thresholds, add a second CC-licensed specimen) and propagate the resulting band widths into the shell measurements.",
        "remediation needed: 1972-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor.py:788-799 and 913-923 — THREE_SYSTEM_PARAMS and the coupling functions tentacle_drive / foot_drive are this implementation's reduced forms (Hill gating sigma^8/(0.6^8+sigma^8), suppression 1/(1+kappa_a a), foot 1/(1+(sigma/0.03)^2)). Digitise Meinhardt (1993) appendix equations (incl. the foot -> source-density negative feedback) and either implement them or tabulate term-by-term where the reduced form departs, with equation numbers in the docstrings and in math_kg_loops.",
        "remediation needed: 1972-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor.py:800 and 1733-1742 — SHELL_DEFAULT_LENGTH_CELLS = 90 is a scale calibration against the specimen's spacing / body length, and the shell still yields 7 tentacles vs 6 while the 1D ring (N_ring = 64, L433-470) selects a different wavelength (10.7 vs 8.1 cells) with the same D_b, D_c. Derive one absolute scale (um per cell) from the specimen's body length and tentacle spacing, use it for BOTH the ring and the shell, and add a D_c sweep on the shell so the audit can see whether kinetics or geometry sets the count." ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.95e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-parameter-expressivity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) & Meinhardt (1993, 2012) Hydra vulgaris activator-inhibitor morphogenesis, head regeneration, tentacle ring & coupled three-system 3D shell — Parameter expressivity: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 sweeps remain (diffusivity ratio across d_c, domain length). Pass 3 adds two sweeps of genuine three-system parameters with monotone, verified effects: the head->tentacle suppression kappa_a in {0, 0.3, 1, 3, 10} shifts the ring centroid basally (0.072 -> 0.122 L, Spearman rho = 1.00) and the kappa_a = 0 ablation lets tentacle activator leak into the hypostome (L1123-1144, Panel E1); the body length L in {64..150} raises the tentacle number 5 -> 10 (rho = 0.97, Panel E2); --shell-length, --shell-steps and --kappa-a are exposed on the CLI (L2008-2010). Deductions: the kappa_a effect on ring position is small (0.05 L over three decades) because the tentacle inhibitor already excludes the apex (-4); the count sweep jumps 5 -> 7 and never produces the specimen's 6 (-3); the tentacle-inhibitor range D_c, the most obvious \"number of tentacles\" knob, is not swept in the shell (in prototyping it changed amplitude but not count), so what controls the count is geometry, not kinetics, and this is not shown (-3); sigma_t, p_t and sigma_f (which set the ring and foot positions) have no sweep or CLI flag (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1972-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor.py L788–L799: sigma_t, p_t, sigma_f, D_c fixed in THREE_SYSTEM_PARAMS without sweep or CLI exposure <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/4d5512d/1972-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor.py#L788-L799>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-parameter-expressivity-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-repro-package> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) & Meinhardt (1993, 2012) Hydra vulgaris activator-inhibitor morphogenesis, head regeneration, tentacle ring & coupled three-system 3D shell — Reproducibility package: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Deterministic seed 1972 throughout; 14-check `--self-test` (L1862-2001) including bitwise determinism of both the 1D solver and the shell solver (FFT + banded solve, L1986-1990), JSON parity, analytic-threshold consistency and every Pass 3 behaviour; CLI documented in argparse; render ~53 s and self-test ~35 s on the pinned venv whose versions are now recorded correctly in this audit. Deductions: no requirements lock file is shipped for this script (-3); the README invocation notes in the dataset describe the model but not the CLI flags or runtimes (-2); `measure_morphoeval()` re-runs the whole ~40 s shell set, and self-test and render each run it again, so a full Pass costs ~2 min of recomputation without caching (-2); matplotlib emits a font-cache warning unless MPLCONFIGDIR is set (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-repro-package-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-repro-package-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-source-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) & Meinhardt (1993, 2012) Hydra vulgaris activator-inhibitor morphogenesis, head regeneration, tentacle ring & coupled three-system 3D shell — Source and data traceability: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "All four DOIs resolve and are repeated in the bib, README and JSON; the specimen, scout manifest and bib stay SHA-256 pinned (L147-176) and the reference JSON's digest is recorded by the measurement sidecar. Pass 3 fixed a real defect: the JSON `hydra_regimes_and_experiments` block had never matched the code and is now in parity and asserted in self-test check 9 (L1922-1943), and the new `three_system_cylindrical_shell` block pins every shell parameter and the firing threshold. Deductions: the reference JSON is still not in EXPECTED_SHA256 (only hashed, L169-172), so it can drift silently between runs (-3); the Pass 3 three-system forms cite Meinhardt (1993) and (2012) without page or equation numbers (-3); the `expected_peak_counts` of the domain sweep are now the observed outputs written back into the JSON (tautological parity) (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/source-traceability" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-source-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-source-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-source-traceability-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-source-traceability-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-specimen-match> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Gierer & Meinhardt (1972) & Meinhardt (1993, 2012) Hydra vulgaris activator-inhibitor morphogenesis, head regeneration, tentacle ring & coupled three-system 3D shell — Morphological realism / specimen match: 87/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The rendered figure now puts the model and the specimen side by side at three levels: the segmented photograph with its 6 tentacles and body axis (Panel C1), the azimuthal luminance profile vs the 1D ring (C2), and in Pass 3 a 3D shell whose silhouette IS the specimen's radius profile, coloured by the three activators (D1), with the unrolled map showing the tentacle ring inside the specimen's attachment band (D2) and the ring position plotted against that band under the kappa_a sweep (E1). The hypostome cap is azimuthally uniform and the foot sits at the basal disc as in the animal. Deductions: the shell gives 7 tentacle primordia where the specimen has 6, and the body length that makes the spacing match is a calibration (L800, L1733-1742) (-5); the ring offset 0.111 is inside but not at the centre of the specimen band 0.070 +- 0.081 (-2); the regenerated hypostome on the wide cut surface is a spot (CV_theta 0.95, E3) unlike the dome of a regenerating polyp (-3); a single specimen photographed obliquely supplies all references, and the attachment radius (23 px) comes from a 0.98 tissue-fraction threshold rather than an anatomical landmark (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1972-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor.py L800–L805: SHELL_DEFAULT_LENGTH_CELLS = 90 is the declared scale calibration; the resulting 7 tentacles vs 6 on the specimen is a mismatch <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/4d5512d/1972-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor.py#L800-L805>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-specimen-match-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gierer-hydra-activator-inhibitor-specimen-match-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.7e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

